{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: amend the contract (amendment 2) to close the gaps lanes A, E and L found, adopting what they already built wherever it is sound, so integration and self-hosting rest on one written contract.","body":{"conditions":"(1) Room lifecycle: a founding route (lane A's POST /v1/rooms and /found) and a route from room name to room id (lane E gap 2). (2) Bearer acts: RoomWire gains lane A's bearerAct; state which acts a bearer may submit and how a bearer client reaches check and roster, or why it cannot (lane E gap 1). (3) Transport: WebSocket authentication (lane E sends the token as subprotocol artroom.token.TOKEN; lane A must accept it), and RPC subscribe returning newline-delimited JSON bytes. (4) MCP: attention returns publishedThrough from RoomApi itself; explain has a structured not-found result instead of null; propose carries because. (5) The invitation link format (lane E: https://HOST/rooms/ROOM/join#i=INVITATION\u0026s=SECRET, secret in the fragment) as a rule. (6) Log entries for policy-activation recompute (reopened obligations) and for land-rule decisions made during preparation, and a retry reason for a reservation-stage byte mismatch (lane A gaps). (7) Lane L gaps: whether log commits are git-signed, checker config digests in policy-activated, and which state verify re-derives (lanes, leases, obligations, landings, delegation grants against grantor role): resolve each or keep it explicitly open with a reason. (8) Changes are additive where possible; the report lists every change that requires edits in lanes A, E or L; npm run typecheck and every package test on Node and workerd pass at the amended head.","target_head":"ca61351fc3a886760b2b7d1d11e241a05b38550e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}